out it; some country recognizers carry high FP risk absent context words; checksum-backed recognizers (cards, IBAN) are the reliable tier. At ~107k chunks the NER pass is the expensive layer of the classification stack (the gitleaks-class regex pass is not), so its scoping is a design question, not a default.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Full Presidio pass over the **internal** tier (where a leak does damage — internal is the broadly-queried tier); **sampled** pass over the secret tier (there PII is expected; the question is calibration, not presence).\n- Runtime/cost at corpus scale on fleet hardware; batching + checkpointing shape.\n- FP review queue: findings land as quarantine candidates (tier-lock upward, never silent delete — per the scanner design in the #6021 research comment), with the matching recognizer + context attached.\n\n## Done looks like\n\nA pass design: recognizer set, tier scoping, cost estimate, review-queue shape.\n\n<!-- agent-note:v1 agent=muse state=filed source=main-chat-2026-11-04-wave2 -->","closed_by":{"login":"developing-today[bot]","id":347365078,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOFLRe1g","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/26439447?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/developing-today","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/developing-today%5Bbot%5D/events{/priva